    <!--
        DEMO-ONLY seed data for tenant_id = 'coca-cola'. Never runs by default —
        every changeSet here is context="demo", and the <include> that pulls
        this file into db.changelog-master.xml is also context="demo", so a
        normal `spring.liquibase.enabled=true` run against any real tenant
        skips all of it. To actually load it (e.g. local dev), activate the
        context explicitly:

            SPRING_LIQUIBASE_CONTEXTS=demo mvn spring-boot:run ...

        IDs are hardcoded, obviously-fake 9-digit values (9000xxxxx) — nowhere
        near the ~18-digit range real SnowflakeIdGenerator output produces —
        specifically so they can never collide with application-generated rows
        and are trivially identifiable/removable.
    -->

